    "id": "q1",
    "text": "What is the shell register map (offset, width, reset value and access of every register)?",
    "default": "Offsets as in registers.map: 0x00 DESIGN_ID, 0x04 BYTE_IN, 0x08 TICK, 0x0C REPLY_LEN, 0x10 REPLY_WORD_SEL, 0x14 REPLY_WORD, 0x18 TELEM_LEN, 0x1C TELEM_WORD_SEL, 0x20 TELEM_WORD, 0x24 TAKE, 0x28 STATUS; all 32-bit.",
    "reason": "The request names these shell registers but gives no offsets.",
    "answer": "IN: offset 0x00, WO, reset 0: [7:0] packet byte, [8] end flag\nSTAT: offset 0x09, RO, reset 0: [0] telemetry on, [1] busy\nRIDX: offset 0x03, RW, reset 0: [6:0] word number\nRWORD: offset 0x04, RO, reset 0: bytes 4i..4i+3 of the reply, first byte on top, zero past the end\nRLEN: offset 0x02, RO, reset 0: length in bytes of the latest reply, 0 if none\nTICK: offset 0x01, WO, reset 0: [7:0] n ticks\nTIDX: offset 0x06, RW, reset 0: [6:0] word number\nTWORD: offset 0x07, RO, reset 0: same for the telemetry frame\nTAKE: offset 0x08, WO, reset 0: any write takes the held telemetry frame\nTLEN: offset 0x05, RO, reset 0: length of the held telemetry frame, 0 if none\nshell: test shell, PROTOCOL.md 1.1\nunmapped: no register at an offset: reads 0, writes ignored (read-only registers behave the same on write)",
